      "topic_id": "construction_perpendicular_from_point",
      "prompt": "Point T is not on line segment DX (length 8 cm). Describe, step by step, how to construct the perpendicular from T to the line DX using only a ruler and a pair of compasses.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "Open the compasses to a radius large enough to reach the line DX from T.",
        "With the compass point on T, draw an arc that crosses DX at two points.",
        "Without changing the compass radius, place the point on each of these two crossing points in turn and draw two more arcs on the far side of DX from T, so that they intersect each other.",
